### Remote Control and Headroom routing are mutually exclusive (2026-07-31, 11:00 PST)

- [x] **[P3]** **Resolved 2026-07-31, 11:00 PST — owner took the second
      branch: Headroom routing is disabled.** The savings did not justify
      routing every request, and its context rewriting was leaking compressed
      system-prompt and usage detail into sessions. Unrouted in four places:
      `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` and the `headroom-guard.sh` `SessionStart` hook
      removed from both `~/.claude/settings.json` and
      `sensebridge/.claude/settings.local.json`; the `# >>> headroom persistent
      env` blocks removed from `~/.zshrc` and `~/.profile`; the Headroom
      provider and MCP blocks removed from `~/.codex/config.toml`. `headroom
      doctor` now reports `claude`, `codex`, and `shell env` as `⚠ not routed`.
      Lifetime savings at cutover, for the record: 2,302,101 tokens / $8.55,
      plus 28,176,916 cache-read tokens / $108.61. Remote Control is therefore
      available again and `remoteControlAtStartup: true` is live config, no
      longer inert — the tidy-up below is moot. The proxy binary, deployment,
      and `~/.claude/hooks/headroom-guard.sh` are left installed so re-enabling
      is a `headroom init claude` away. Historical detail below.

      `claude doctor`'s only
      remaining warning, and `headroom doctor`'s only non-passing row, were the
      same finding: Remote Control requires `api.anthropic.com`, and Headroom
      works by pointing `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` at `http://127.0.0.1:8787`. The
      constraint is hard-coded in the Claude Code binary
      (`~/.local/share/claude/versions/2.1.220` contains the string verbatim:
      "Remote Control is only available when using Claude via
      api.anthropic.com"). There is no localhost exemption, and `headroom wrap
      claude` does not rescue it — it sets the same variable.

      So it is strictly either/or:

      - **Keep `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` (current, recommended).** Headroom's
        rewriting keeps saving tokens on every request; Remote Control stays
        unavailable. Note `remoteControlAtStartup: true` is currently in
        `~/.claude/settings.json` and is therefore inert config — harmless, but
        misleading to a future reader.
      - **Drop it and start sessions via `headroom wrap claude` per project.**
        Remote Control works in unwrapped sessions; Headroom only applies where
        you remember to wrap.

      No action is required to stay on the current branch — the warning is
      expected and correct. If the recommended branch is confirmed, the tidy-up
      is to remove the inert `remoteControlAtStartup` key.

