        `docs:build` renders `docs/` to `tmp/_site` under the **same
        `github-pages` gem bundle** the Pages action runs (Jekyll 3.10 pin), in
        a `ruby:3.3-slim` container, so nothing installs on the host; `a11y`
        builds and then runs the existing gate, installing `pa11y`/`puppeteer`
        on demand (still `--no-save`). Gems persist in `tmp/docs-jekyll/`, so
        only the first run pays the native-extension compile.
        **Verified: 22 pages, both themes, 1058 interactive elements named,
        all checks passed.**
      - `npm --prefix website run test:a11y` → new
        [`website/scripts/a11y.js`](website/scripts/a11y.js). The objection is
        answered rather than accepted: the preview server runs **in the gate's
        own process** via Astro's programmatic `preview()`, not as a child, so
        the listening socket is owned by that PID and the kernel closes it
        however the run ends. There is no crash window that can strand 4321.
        An already-running `npm run preview` is detected and reused.
        **Verified: 8/8 URLs, 0 errors, on both the in-process and the
        reuse path; port confirmed released after a `SIGKILL` with no cleanup.**

