### CI/security automation audit (2026-07-27)

- [x] **[P2]** `dependabot.yml`'s grouped PRs (`dev-dependencies` group, e.g.
      #44 "dev-dependencies group with 2 updates", #45 "...in /website with 4
      updates") never auto-merge even when every member update is
      patch/minor. Root cause: `dependabot/fetch-metadata` can't report a
      single `update-type` for a grouped PR (known upstream limitation), so
      `dependabot-automerge.yml`'s
      `steps.meta.outputs.update-type == 'version-update:semver-patch' ||
      ...-minor'` condition never matches a grouped PR. Fix needs a design
      decision, not a quick patch: either stop grouping dev-dependencies (loses
      the batching benefit) or switch the workflow's gate to something that
      inspects each dependency in the group (e.g.
      `steps.meta.outputs.dependency-names` + per-dep version comparison, or
      GitHub's newer `dependency-group` output plus a stricter allowlist).
      **Done 2026-08-05** — owner decided (interview) to keep grouping and gate
      per-dependency instead. `.github/workflows/dependabot-automerge.yml` now
      adds a "Check every dependency is patch or minor" step that parses
      `steps.meta.outputs.updated-dependencies-json` (the pinned
      `dependabot/fetch-metadata@25dd0e34f...` v3 SHA already exposes it, no
      version bump needed — confirmed against the action's `v3` README/source)
      with `jq`, requiring `all()` per-dependency `updateType` to be
      `semver-patch` or `semver-minor`; the existing auto-merge step now gates
      on that boolean instead of the group-wide `update-type` output. Verified:
      `npm run lint:actions` (actionlint) passes clean; traced the `jq` filter
      locally against a synthetic all-patch/minor payload (→ `true`) and a
      payload with one `semver-major` entry (→ `false`), matching the
      dev-dependencies-group and /website-group shapes from #44/#45. **Not
      verified end-to-end** — this needs a real grouped Dependabot PR to
      confirm `updated-dependencies-json` is actually populated as documented
      and that the automerge step fires; no live PR was run this session.

- [x] **[P1]** The `dependabot-automerge.yml` fix (repo settings: enabled
      `allow_auto_merge` + "Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull
      requests") is confirmed working end-to-end.
      **Done/Fixed 2026-08-06** — the CI failures that were blocking merge
      (`Secret scan (GitGuardian)`, `Deploy to Railway preview`,
      `Build + smoke-test docker/Dockerfile`,
      `Stylelint + ESLint + Prettier + typecheck + build`) all pass on
      current dependabot PRs (`gh pr checks 64`, `gh pr checks 65`); PRs
      #46/#47/#49 are closed/superseded, and #60/#61 auto-merged cleanly via
      `app/github-actions` (`gh pr view 60 --json autoMergeRequest,mergedBy`).

