### Admin dashboard setup — Next.js + WakaTime (2026-07-27)

**Decision (2026-07-27):** Next.js, not Astro, for the admin dashboard.
`website/` is deliberately static/zero-JS/content-first (see
[`docs/TOOLING.md`](docs/TOOLING.md)); an admin dashboard is the opposite
profile — dynamic, behind auth, all interactive widgets, no SEO/zero-JS
constraint — so it should be a **separate app**, not bolted onto `website/`.
Next.js API routes/middleware handle auth and keep the WakaTime API key
server-side.

- [x] **[P3]** Scaffold a new Next.js app (outside `website/`, e.g.
      `admin/`) for the dashboard — decide hosting (Vercel, same as
      `website/`?) and auth approach (single-owner login) before scaffolding.
      **Done 2026-08-12** — built (owner chose the full scaffold, this session). `admin/` is a
      Next.js 16 App Router app, deliberately outside `website/`, with no database,
      no write path, and no background jobs — every tile is a live read behind a
      short TTL cache. Three tiles: WakaTime (`WAKATIME_API_KEY`, falling back to
      `~/.wakatime.cfg`), Sentry (read-scoped `event:read`/`project:read`/`org:read`
      token, server-side route handler only), and dev tooling
      (`rtk gain --format json`, caveman, ponytail). Auth is a single-owner Basic
      gate in `proxy.ts` that **fails closed** — unset or under-16-character
      `ADMIN_PASSWORD` serves 503 rather than running open — with a constant-time
      compare, since Edge has no `timingSafeEqual`. No secret is `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` or
      reaches a client bundle; responses are `private, no-store`; CSP,
      `frame-ancestors 'none'`, and `noindex` are set; upstream calls have an 8s
      timeout and no retries. Every tile fails soft. **Verified:** `npm run check`
      in `admin/` — typecheck, build, and a 15-case HTTP smoke test
      (`admin/scripts/smoke.mjs`) that starts the real production server and
      asserts the 503, 401, near-miss-password, 200, gated-API, CSP, and
      fail-soft-tile paths. `admin/README.md` documents the scope and why it runs
      locally.

- [x] **[P3]** Wire in WakaTime: start with the public embed/share widgets
      (`wakatime.com/share/@user/...` — SVG badges/charts, no API key
      needed) before building a custom API-route + chart integration. The
      WakaTime API key already lives at `~/.wakatime.cfg`
      ([`docs/TOOLING.md`](docs/TOOLING.md)) — if a custom integration is
      built later, read it server-side only, never in a client bundle.
