      in `admin/` — typecheck, build, and a 15-case HTTP smoke test
      (`admin/scripts/smoke.mjs`) that starts the real production server and
      asserts the 503, 401, near-miss-password, 200, gated-API, CSP, and
      fail-soft-tile paths. `admin/README.md` documents the scope and why it runs
      locally.

      **Correction to this item's own premise:** caveman has **no** savings data on
      disk. `~/.claude/.caveman-history.jsonl` does not exist (checked 2026-08-12);
      what the plugin writes is `.caveman-active` and `.caveman-mode-log.jsonl`, and
      neither carries token counts. So no sync step is needed and none was built —
      the tile shows the level and says plainly that there is nothing to total.
      ponytail is handled as this item specified: the `ponytail:` debt count, never
      a fabricated savings percent.

