### Awareness camera preview + object highlights (2026-07-27, 00:30 PST)

- [x] **[P2]** **Detected-object labels are still English-only.** The outline
      captions inherit the same Vision-identifier limitation already documented
      on `ObjectClassificationService` — a user running the app in Spanish or
      Vietnamese now *reads* the English noun as well as hearing it. Same root
      cause, same open question, no new work needed until that one is answered.
      **Done 2026-08-12** — the mechanism is built and the answer to the open question is a
      curated table (owner decision, this session). New `SpokenVocabulary` holds
      article-first phrases for ~75 identifiers a real walk produces — furniture,
      structure, people, animals, vehicles, kitchen, electronics, carried objects,
      outdoors, plus the **complete** `BuiltInSoundClassifier.targetClassNames`
      set. `SpokenPhrase.subject(for:locale:)` resolves most-specific-locale-first
      and falls back to the **English phrase**, never the raw identifier, so an
      unlisted identifier degrades the language and never the accuracy. Whole
      phrases rather than article + noun, because Spanish gender agreement and
      Vietnamese classifiers are not derivable from an English identifier.
      `locale` is threaded through `ObjectClassificationService`,
      `SoundClassificationRunner`, `BuiltInSoundClassifier`, and
      `CustomSoundClassifier`. **Fixed three real bugs along the way:**
      `LabelingView`, `SceneDescriptionView`, and `SoundAlertsView` were all
      hedging in the *process* locale rather than the language chosen in Settings,
      so a user who picked Español heard an English sentence. **Verified:** 6 new
      unit tests (translation, English fallback, regional-before-bare ordering,
      every entry covers es+vi, every sound class covered); package suite 174/174;
      device build green. **Still open — folded into the native-speaker review item:**
      the wording is seeded, not reviewed. A reviewer changing an entry changes only
      that entry.

