      string with no deep link to Settings — consider
      `UIApplication.openSettingsURLString` once a second permission-gated
      feature makes the pattern worth extracting.
      **Done 2026-08-12** — done, and at the root rather than on this one screen. Four screens
      carried the same dead end ("Enable it in Settings" with no way to get there),
      so the fix is one shared `OpenSettingsButton` used by Read, Identify,
      Describe, and Sounds. It appears only after a permission is actually denied —
      `OpenSettingsButton.canResolve(_:)` matches camera/microphone
      `authorizationDenied` and nothing else, so a missing camera or a failed
      capture does not send anyone on a pointless trip. The flag is cleared at the
      start of each attempt, so granting the permission retires the button. That
      dead end costs a VoiceOver user far more than a sighted one, which is why the
      "wait for a second permission-gated feature" condition in this item is met
      four times over. **Verified:** device build green, full simulator suite green.

