      for `thermalState`/`ProcessInfo` — no hits outside an unrelated UI-test
      helper. The existing "Battery and thermal, re-measured..." and
      "Battery and thermal over a real walk" items elsewhere in this file
      (search `battery and thermal`) are about *measuring* drain and
      throttling on a real walk — device validation, not code. This item is
      the missing code-side mitigation those measurements would validate:
      nothing today reduces camera/depth/inference workload when
      `ProcessInfo.thermalState` reports `.serious`/`.critical`. Reasonable
      to scope together with those existing device-validation items once
      someone is holding the device, but the behavior itself doesn't exist to
      validate yet.
      **Done 2026-08-12** — built. New `ThermalBackoff` in `SenseBridgeCore/Sensing/` maps
      `ProcessInfo.thermalState` to three levels and an interval multiplier
      (`.nominal`/`.fair` → 1×, `.serious` → 2×, `.critical` → 4×), applied to both
      the 750 ms depth cadence and the narration cadence in
      `AmbientAwarenessSession`. Every level change is spoken once, recovery
      included — a degraded cadence the user is not told about is indistinguishable
      from the app having stopped. It never stops the session: silence mid-walk is
      worse than a slower cadence that was announced. Three new `en`/`es`/`vi`
      catalog strings (insertion-only). **Verified:** 6 new unit tests over the
      policy (including a guard that no multiplier is < 1, and a doctrine test that
      no notice claims anything about the world); package suite 174/174; device
      build green. **Not verified:** actual thermal behaviour on a hot device —
      that is the existing device-validation item.

- [x] **[P3]** **Configurable spoken-output verbosity.** Source:
